    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.statusline\n\n### Question\n\nHy, i am new here. I would like to know if there is a way to see where errors are in a file in my statusline (for example, line of the first error).\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2659d4c1-3a01-4304-bad7-e2653d0a0b7c)\r\n\r\nAs i understand it right now \"E4\" means there are 4 errors, but on top of that I would like to know if I can see the actual lines.\r\n\r\nThank you.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.statusline</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hy, i am new here. I would like to know if there is a way to see where errors are in a file in my statusline (for example, line of the first error).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/93163183/404551677-2659d4c1-3a01-4304-bad7-e2653d0a0b7c.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..cMIhBdHQG--wQAAhdKHECcaWb2oLaCpKSbnMqTbZekw\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/93163183/404551677-2659d4c1-3a01-4304-bad7-e2653d0a0b7c.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..cMIhBdHQG--wQAAhdKHECcaWb2oLaCpKSbnMqTbZekw\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As i understand it right now \"E4\" means there are 4 errors, but on top of that I would like to know if I can see the actual lines.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thank you.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.statusline\nQuestion\nHy, i am new here. I would like to know if there is a way to see where errors are in a file in my statusline (for example, line of the first error).\n\nAs i understand it right now \"E4\" means there are 4 errors, but on top of that I would like to know if I can see the actual lines.\nThank you.",
